{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And I will hide My face from them and it shall be for devouring</b> ס\"ת (end-letters) in gematria = המן. And this is what they expounded in Hullin: 'I will surely hide' — an allusion to Esther:" "<b>ומצאהו</b> defective vav, to say that they were exiled six times. Three by Sennacherib. And three by Nebuzaradan:" "<b>הרעות האלה</b> in gematria = four exiles:"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {0 "The reference is to the end-letters of the phrase, whose combined gematria equals המן. He alludes to the Talmudic discussion (Hullin 139b) connecting Esther's name to divine concealment.", 1 "He reads the defective spelling (missing vav) as hinting at six (ו״י = 6) instances of exile."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:11:10.852105340Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}